  "question": {
    "text": "<math><mn>10.30</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is dissolved into a liter of sea water of density <math><mn>1.03</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math> . The concentration of <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> in ppm is _____________.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "10",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Formula of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ppm</mi></math>&nbsp;is-</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ppm</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>weight</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>of</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>solute</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>weight</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>of</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>solution</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup></math></p><p><math><mi>p</mi><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>10.3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1030</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></math> =10</p><p>PPM is a concentration term and its full form is &quot;parts per million&quot; and it also can be expressed as milligrams per liter (mg/L). This measurement is the mass of a chemical or contaminate per unit volume of water.</p>",
    "image": null
